## 1. Modeling the Logic (The Correct Implementation)
For a payout request to be valid, the amount x must satisfy both conditions simultaneously. In propositional logic, this is a conjunction ($\land$): [1] 
$$P(x) = (x \ge 105) \land (x \le 500000)$$ 
If P(x) is True, the system allows the payout. If it is False, it triggers an error.
